WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.070
Welcome to the Lobo Infinity Portal. This
walkthrough shows you how to find a game,

00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:08.858
prepare for it, submit your result, and
explore the community.

00:00:08.858 --> 00:00:14.846
On the dashboard, scroll to Choose Your
First Move. These three cards take you to
Army

00:00:14.846 --> 00:00:20.207
Intelligence, a battle report, or the events
page. Public browsing is open to

00:00:20.207 --> 00:00:20.834
everyone.

00:00:20.834 --> 00:00:26.138
Select All Events in the sidebar. Open the
event you want to join and check its

00:00:26.138 --> 00:00:31.374
registration status. For casual games, use
the Game Network or find players on

00:00:31.374 --> 00:00:31.911
Discord.

00:00:31.911 --> 00:00:37.009
Use the event selector in the sidebar to
choose your competition. The links below it

00:00:37.009 --> 00:00:42.228
lead to that event. In Standings, choose
your division to see the players and
recorded

00:00:42.228 --> 00:00:42.653
scores.

00:00:42.653 --> 00:00:48.254
Before arranging a league game, open Mission
and Map. Check the date range, the active

00:00:48.254 --> 00:00:53.790
missions, and the assigned maps. View
Mission opens the scenario details from
Mission

00:00:53.790 --> 00:00:54.181
Geist.

00:00:54.181 --> 00:00:59.739
Open the T T S Map Library to preview
tables. Scroll down to search by map name,

00:00:59.739 --> 00:01:05.713
filter by named mission setup, or sort by
highest rated. Check the collection for your

00:01:05.713 --> 00:01:06.130
event.

00:01:06.130 --> 00:01:11.374
Open a table card to inspect its terrain.
The overhead view shows the layout, and the

00:01:11.374 --> 00:01:16.618
angled view shows heights and cover. Use the
Workshop collection link, then match the

00:01:16.618 --> 00:01:17.852
bag name shown here.

00:01:17.852 --> 00:01:23.364
After playing, select Submit Game. Choose
the form that matches your game: League,

00:01:23.364 --> 00:01:28.942
Team Tournament, Casual, or Top Forty. Each
button opens its own Google Form. Check

00:01:28.942 --> 00:01:32.236
your scores with your opponent before
submitting.

00:01:32.236 --> 00:01:37.880
Open Battle Reports to browse recorded
games. Each row shows the players, mission,
and

00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:41.424
scores. Click the game number to open the
full report.

00:01:41.424 --> 00:01:46.490
The report shows the objective points,
tournament points, and victory points.
Scroll

00:01:46.490 --> 00:01:50.833
for the mission summary, map, highlights,
and review. Battle stories are

00:01:50.833 --> 00:01:55.718
fictionalized; use the recorded results and
player notes for the factual account.

00:01:55.718 --> 00:02:01.484
Open Army Intelligence. Choose a faction or
sectorial, or try the Corregidor example.

00:02:01.484 --> 00:02:06.708
This page explores submitted lists, common
profiles, specialist coverage, and

00:02:06.708 --> 00:02:07.929
battlefield roles.

00:02:07.929 --> 00:02:13.499
Use Combat, Defense, Control, or All to
browse tactical roles. Read the exact weapon

00:02:13.499 --> 00:02:19.202
and linked status next to each rating. The
global percentile shows its standing in the

00:02:19.202 --> 00:02:22.849
wider benchmark, while usage describes
submitted lists.

00:02:22.849 --> 00:02:27.877
Open Factions to explore armies and
sectorials through their recorded league
results.

00:02:27.877 --> 00:02:32.964
Scroll to the army you want, then open its
card for a closer look. Read the game count

00:02:32.964 --> 00:02:37.696
alongside its record and win rate: these
describe games submitted to the portal.

00:02:37.696 --> 00:02:42.796
Open Players to browse the community. Use
the event filter for All Events or a

00:02:42.796 --> 00:02:48.158
specific competition. Each card shows a
player’s division, game count, and record.

00:02:48.158 --> 00:02:53.324
Open a card to view their profile, then
scroll to Game History to explore their

00:02:53.324 --> 00:02:54.305
recorded games.

00:02:54.305 --> 00:02:59.592
Open Missions and choose an event, or leave
All Events selected. View Mission opens

00:02:59.592 --> 00:03:04.689
the available scenario details. Click a
mission name for its analysis, including

00:03:04.689 --> 00:03:10.040
recorded games, first-turn win rate, faction
performance, and recent battle reports.

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:13.289
Read the number of games alongside each
percentage.

00:03:13.289 --> 00:03:19.141
Open Lobo’s Little Helper for the updated
guide and Discord link. In Discord, start

00:03:19.141 --> 00:03:24.781
with slash help. Use slash list analyse with
an Army code for a readable roster,

00:03:24.781 --> 00:03:30.351
legality summary, and two D Tabletop
Simulator export. Tactical Brief, Ratings,

00:03:30.351 --> 00:03:36.344
Classifieds, and T T S Notes open privately
through buttons. Use slash combat matchup

00:03:36.344 --> 00:03:42.195
to compare two profiles, slash combat
counters for reactive answers, and slash
play

00:03:42.195 --> 00:03:44.663
for availability and game requests.

00:03:44.663 --> 00:03:50.317
You are ready to use the portal. Find an
event or an opponent, check your mission and

00:03:50.317 --> 00:03:55.438
map, play your game, and submit the result.
Return for reports, rankings, and

00:03:55.438 --> 00:03:57.500
inspiration for your next list.
